From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: data channel: skip a lost packet while waiting; never let the window fill completely

A single lost packet while the worker is idle (the normal state when the
decoder keeps up: window size 0-2) wedged the data channel for 10-20 s. The
worker calls IHS_SessionPacketsWindowDiscard only at the top of its outer
loop, then sits in an inner `while (!Poll) CondWait` loop; Poll fails on the
gap at the head and Discard, the only thing that can step the head over a gap,
never runs again. Packets pile up behind the gap until the ring holds
capacity-1 of them, at which point IHS_SessionPacketsWindowSize() reads 0
(tail.pos + 1 == head.pos means both "empty" and "every slot occupied"), the
next packet is written into the gap slot and delivered out of order (the
"Unexpected video frame sequence N (expect M)" with N-M ~ 2048), every later
packet maps onto an occupied slot and is dropped as a "dup" with the tail
frozen, and only ~3x capacity packets later does the far-ahead check reset the
window ("items overflow (available 2048)": full, not drained). When that reset
re-adds a mid-frame fragment as the new head the window wedges again for
another 2048 packets. At 300-550 video packets/s a lost packet costs 10-20 s
of frozen video while audio (its own window, 10x fewer packets) plays on. The
official client drops the incomplete frame and asks for a keyframe at once.

Run Discard before every Poll (the loop returns to its top after each wake),
so a gap at the head is skipped as soon as a newer frame head exists; an
incomplete frame still gets DISCARD_DIFF (200 ms) for late fragments. Reject
an add that would occupy the last free slot so Size() is never ambiguous (a
real backlog now trips the overflow reset at capacity-1 with a truthful
"available 1"). Treat a packet exactly Size() behind the tail as already
processed: it maps to the slot just before the head, where it was orphaned and
later made a new packet look like a duplicate.

diff -ru a/src/session/channels/ch_data.c b/src/session/channels/ch_data.c
--- a/src/session/channels/ch_data.c
+++ b/src/session/channels/ch_data.c
@@ -134,12 +134,12 @@
         if (discarded > 0) {
             IHS_SessionLog(channel->base.session, IHS_LogLevelDebug, channelName, "Discarded %u packets", discarded);
         }
-        bool hasFrame;
-        while (!(hasFrame = IHS_SessionPacketsWindowPoll(channel->window, &frame))) {
+        /* No frame yet: wait for the next packet, then go round again so Discard runs before
+         * the next Poll. Discard is what steps the head over a packet that never arrives;
+         * polling alone waits on such a gap forever. */
+        bool hasFrame = IHS_SessionPacketsWindowPoll(channel->window, &frame);
+        if (!hasFrame) {
             IHS_CondWait(channel->windowCond, channel->windowLock);
-            if (channel->interrupted) {
-                break;
-            }
         }
         IHS_MutexUnlock(channel->windowLock);
         if (hasFrame) {
